From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhishek Kekane <akekane@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 07:41:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Block restricted hosts when adding HTTP image locations

Apply import_filtering_opts to HTTP(S) locations and validate
the URI before contacting the backend, so location add cannot
SSRF glance-api into loopback or link-local targets.

On stable/2025.1, FunctionalTest location fixtures whitelist
127.0.0.1/localhost via self.allowed_hosts because self.config()
does not affect the API subprocess.

OSISM: rebased onto the 2024.1 code base from the 2024.2 series
(osism/container-images-kolla#790), with one deliberate omission. glance
28.x has no add-location API -- POST /v2/images/{id}/locations arrived in
2024.2 -- so the hunk adding the restricted-host check to add_location(),
its unit test and its functional test are dropped; there is no such entry
point on 2024.1 to harden. Everything that does apply is kept unchanged:
the switch to validate_uri() in the web-download path, the pre-backend
validation in _check_location_uri() that also covers the older
PATCH /locations route, the store_utils and common/utils changes, and the
test_update_locations_blocks_restricted_http_hosts functional test.

Closes-Bug: #2161330
SecurityImpact

Conflicts:
  glance/common/scripts/utils.py
  glance/tests/functional/v2/test_images.py
  glance/tests/unit/v2/test_images_resource.py

